"String 型別，最長 127 bytes。多數物聯網卡留空": "String type, up to 127 bytes. Leave it empty for most IoT SIMs",
"TCP client 收發。本組全部走 buffer 模式（QIOPEN 末參數 0）—— ⚠ 收到的資料「不會」自己出現在終端機：模組只發一則 +QIURC: \"recv\",<id> 通知，要自己按 Read Data（AT+QIRD）才取得出來，而且要重複讀到回 +QIRD: 0 為止，否則模組不會再發下一次通知。收不到通知就先查 Hardware 頁的 AT+QURCCFG=\"urcport\" 是不是 uart1 —— 不是的話 URC 全跑到 USB 埠去了。另外，預設對端 tcpbin.com 是「以行為單位」的 echo 伺服器，送出的資料結尾沒有換行（hex 0A）它就一直緩衝著不回送（實測：不加 0A 等 6 秒無回應，補一個 0A 後 0.1 秒立刻收到）。": "TCP client send and receive. Everything in this group runs in buffer mode (last QIOPEN parameter 0) — ⚠ incoming data does NOT show up in the terminal by itself: the module emits a single +QIURC: \"recv\",<id> notification, and you have to press Read Data (AT+QIRD) yourself to fetch it, repeating the read until it returns +QIRD: 0 — otherwise the module will never issue the next notification. If no notification arrives, first check whether AT+QURCCFG=\"urcport\" on the Hardware page is set to uart1 — if it is not, every URC is going out of the USB port instead. Also, the default peer tcpbin.com is a \"line-oriented\" echo server: unless the data you send ends with a newline (hex 0A) it just keeps buffering and sends nothing back (measured: without 0A, 6 s passed with no response at all; after appending a single 0A it came back within 0.1 s).",
"TCP keepalive：啟用；閒置 {0} 秒開始探測、每 {1} 秒一次、最多 {2} 次": "TCP keepalive: enabled; probing starts after {0} s idle, once every {1} s, up to {2} times",
"TCP 層的保活探測（手冊 §2.3.1 AT+QICFG=\"tcp/keepalive\"）。⚠ 對 tcpbin.com 的 15 秒閒置逾時「完全沒用」—— 實測開了 keepalive 仍然在 15.1 秒被關：keepalive 送的是 TCP 層的空探測封包，應用程式根本看不到，而 tcpbin 數的是「有沒有收到應用資料」；何況 interval_time 最小 25 秒，本來就大於 15 秒。要撐過應用層逾時只能送真資料（例如每 10 秒 AT+QISENDEX=0,\"0A\" 送一個換行）。它真正有用的地方是「電信商 NAT 保活與偵測死連線」—— IoT 卡的 NAT 對應閒置數分鐘就會被回收，那是另一個層次的斷線。參數範圍取自手冊；按 QICFG=? 可看這顆韌體實際回報的範圍（零流量）。": "TCP-layer keepalive probing (manual §2.3.1 AT+QICFG=\"tcp/keepalive\"). ⚠ Against tcpbin.com's 15 s idle timeout it is \"completely useless\" — measured with keepalive on, the connection was still closed at 15.1 s: keepalive sends empty probe packets at the TCP layer, which the application never sees, while tcpbin counts \"has any application data arrived\"; and interval_time has a minimum of 25 s anyway, already longer than 15 s. The only way to survive an application-layer timeout is to send real data (for example a newline every 10 s with AT+QISENDEX=0,\"0A\"). Where it genuinely helps is \"keeping the carrier's NAT mapping alive and detecting dead connections\" — the NAT mapping of an IoT SIM is reclaimed after a few idle minutes, which is a disconnection at another level. The parameter ranges come from the manual; press QICFG=? to see the ranges this firmware actually reports (no traffic).",
